      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_fc3a130d",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: american_soldiers_praying_in_jesus_name; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts American soldiers in uniform, seemingly praying, with overlaid text that reads 'american soldiers praying in jesus name' and 'that they don't have to go overseas for the holidays.' The overall intent is to mock or satirize the soldiers' religious devotion by framing it as a selfish wish to avoid deployment, thereby implying hypocrisy or insensitivity. This juxtaposition of solemn religious imagery with a cynical, self-serving wish undermines the perceived seriousness of their faith and service. While not explicitly targeting a specific protected group with hate, the meme is harmful because it trivializes the gravity of military service and religious practice, potentially offending those who view the soldiers' prayers as genuine expressions of patriotism and faith. The meme's intent is to provoke laughter through irony, but it risks causing offense and disrespect toward service members and their beliefs, making it a harmful piece of content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_03212f61"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
